        "title": "Nice scenery and culturally interesting",
        "text": "A strange combination of religious funeral site and tourist attraction. Entrance fee for non-SAARC (\"Western\") 1000 rupees or about 10 dollar. For that price you can walk around Pashtupatinath indefinitely. And it's a big place!  There are multiple temples and religious buildings within the park and hills, and also a deer sanctuary. Know that some temples are destroyes though and others are only accessible for hindus. Still definitely worth a visit though. The cremations seem to take place virtually everyday and you are bound to witness one if you stick around the river area (the ghats). When you go further up one of the hills you will find the more quiet parts, where monkeys and local Shiva devotees go to hang out. One of the more interesting places to visit in KTM!",
        "review_tip": null,
